{
  "_notes": [
    "Iron Man Vault Edition, code 1.86 (im_186ve). Same board and game_state as im_185ve: every field",
    "below was re-measured on a 663-sample live recording (2026-09-15, HDP) spanning an operator-menu",
    "session, coins, one five-ball game with a mid-ball tilt on ball 1, and attract, and matched the",
    "1.85 map byte for byte -- ball 0x00034DB9, player 0x00034DB8, status 0x00034DEA (1/20/22, tilted",
    "for the 15 samples from the tilt to the end of ball 1), scores at 0x021109E4, credits 0x0211100C,",
    "volume 0x02110248 with complement, adjustment records 32/34/35/39 and Replay Type at 12.",
    "What moved between 1.85 and 1.86 is the champion storage: the five high-score records and the",
    "eight mode-champion records sit 16 bytes later (0x02102C18 and 0x02102CB8 instead of 0x02102C08",
    "and 0x02102CA8), as does the default-threshold table (0x021022A8, stride 0x18). On 1.86 the 1.85",
    "addresses read 0xFF, so the two revisions need separate maps. Record format is unchanged: three",
    "initials, 0xFF fill, score at +24, checksum16 (0xFFFF minus the sum of the first 28 bytes) at +28.",
    "Mode champion labels are the attract order (Bogey, Iron Man, War Machine, Iron Monger, Whiplash,",
    "Drones, Jericho, Do Or Die Multiball); the record order matches the threshold table (six",
    "5,000,000, then 10,000,000, then 25,000,000) as on 1.85.",
    "The non-Vault im_186 does NOT share this map: its NVRAM side (scores, credits, volume, adjustment",
    "records, champion records) matches, but the CPU-side ball, player and status bytes live elsewhere;",
    "see im_186.map.json."
  ],
